language ESSENCE' 1.0
$ Someone in Dreadsbury Mansion killed Aunt Agatha. Persons: 0 = Agatha herself, 1 = the butler, 2 = Charles. Find the killer.
find killer : int(0..2)
$ hates[p, x] is true when person p hates person x
find hates : matrix indexed by [int(0..2), int(0..2)] of bool
$ richer[p, x] is true when person p is richer than person x
find richer : matrix indexed by [int(0..2), int(0..2)] of bool

branching on [killer, hates, richer]

such that
$ a killer always hates his victim, Agatha (person 0)
hates[killer, 0] = true,
$ a killer is no richer than his victim
!richer[killer, 0],
$ Agatha hates everybody except the butler
forAll x : int(0..2) . (hates[0, x] <-> (x != 1)),
$ the butler hates everyone whom Agatha hates
forAll x : int(0..2) . (hates[0, x] -> hates[1, x]),
$ Charles hates no one that Agatha hates
forAll x : int(0..2) . (hates[0, x] -> !hates[2, x]),
$ the butler hates everyone not richer than Aunt Agatha
forAll x : int(0..2) . (!richer[x, 0] -> hates[1, x]),
$ no one hates everyone
forAll p : int(0..2) . exists x : int(0..2) . !hates[p, x]
